<section class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">OUR PURPOSE</span><h1>Health support rooted in Ubuntu.</h1><p>Ubuntu Health AI is a digital-health prototype intended to make basic health education and care navigation easier to access.</p></section>
<div class="content-card"><h2>Project goals</h2><ul class="nice-list"><li>Share understandable health education.</li><li>Help users recognize general warning signs and seek appropriate care.</li><li>Provide a simple way to request follow-up from a health facility.</li><li>Encourage respectful, accessible, privacy-aware digital health services.</li></ul><h2>What this project is not</h2><p>It is not a diagnostic device, a medical record system, an emergency service, or a replacement for qualified clinicians. The symptom guidance and chatbot are rule-based demonstration features and have not been clinically validated.</p><h2>Next development priorities</h2><p>Clinician review, verified facility directory, authentication and permissions, privacy and security assessment, accessibility testing, and a clear process for responding to appointment requests.</p></div>
